one two three four  there's been so many times where we're  told that movies are just make-believe  but that's not always the case not  everything in the movies we watch  is fabricated in fact the filmmakers and  stars of many of your favorite films  will often go to extreme lengths to make  their films feel as real as possible  from shaving one's head to skydiving  this is when what happened on screen  actually happened on set oh i love it  martin scorsese's award-winning black  comedy is one of the craziest  and most memorable movies to date and  for good reasons  during the film's notorious office party  scene involving an almost naked marching  band  one of the things that can be seen in  the background is a woman getting her  hair completely shaved off her head  what you may not know is that actually  happened on set  the name of the woman is natasha newman  a hair stylist and long time friend of  star leonardo dicaprio  newman actually volunteered for her head  to be shaved something that surprised  the film's producers  [Applause]  ratatouille is one of pixar's most  beloved films though what you may not  know  is some of the lengths that some of the  creative team took to make a film about  a talking rat who can cook  a bit more real for the scene where  linguine dives into a river in his  chef's uniform to rescue remy  the animation team wanted to figure out  what parts of the outfit would stick to  the body  this led to crew member kesten migdal to  dress as a cook and jump into a pool  in order for the crew to make the  animation feel more realistic  but we're together on this pixar's soul  is one of their most philosophical films  yet  and despite the fantastical world built  in the film the filmmakers wanted to  make sure that it could still have some  accuracy  the first soul that is counted in the  film is 108 billion  210 million 121 415  the writers of this pixar hit had  actually consulted with the population  reference bureau  to get this number meaning that there  really has been over 108 billion humans  in the history of the planet  soul number 108 billion two hundred ten  million one hundred twenty one thousand  four hundred and fifteen friends is  arguably one of the most well-known  sitcoms of all time  and it's clear just how passionate the  cast was when the show was on air  in the season seven episode of the show  titled the one with joey's new brain  we learned that ross actually plays the  bagpipes what you may not know is that  actor david schwimmer  actually learned to play the bagpipes  for the episode to top that off in the  scene where ross plays for phoebe and  rachel  jennifer aniston went off script and  started giggling as lisa kudrow sang  along to the sound of ross's bagpipes  bagpipes are appropriate for our wedding  why not because we hate them working  with child actors can be difficult  such was the case with the creative team  behind monsters inc  when trying to get five-year-old mary  gibbs to record her lines for the iconic  role of  boo they eventually found an effective  solution  instead of having gibbs stuck in a  recording booth the crew followed her  around with a microphone  and recorded her talking as she played  the results were spectacular with  audiences  all over the world falling in love with  boo  what the notebook is arguably the most  popular nicholas sparks movie to date  and starred ryan gosling and rachel  mcadams  just as they were becoming a-list stars  gosling decided to go with his role as  noah and just like the character he  decided to start building furniture  the same furniture that gosling built  was actually used in the film for the  scene  set in the house that noah built for  ally i'm a married woman  not yet stockard channing's rizzo is a  favorite among fans of the hit musical  grease  though fans may be surprised to learn  that the hickeys she has throughout the  film  are actually real the hickeys were  created by jeff conaway who played  channing's on-screen boyfriend kaniki  conaway told the film's crew that a  hickey from kenickie had to be given by  him  from me pinkie lee this oscar-nominated  true life thriller  is quite the intense experience the  pivotal scene which features hank's  title character being treated by a medic  after being rescued from the somalian  pirates  is one of the film's most  heart-wrenching scenes director paul  greengrass went the extra mile when  directing the scene  by casting danielle albert an actual  navy medic  greengrass had told albert to treat the  scene as a regular military exercise  leading the scene to be entirely  improvised can you tell me what's going  on  in the climactic concert scene of the  hit 2003 comedy freaky friday  we see jamie lee curtis rocking out on  the guitar  but just like david schwimmer playing  the bagpipes curtis  actually was playing the guitar on the  screen while doing  press for the film curtis claimed that  learning to play the guitar was one of  her favorite parts about making the film  this ultimately paid off as curtis's  performance in the film  won over critics and audiences alike and  even earned her several award  nominations  well what am i supposed to do margot  robbie received universal acclaim for  her oscar-nominated performance as  disgraced figure skater tanya harding  robbie was extremely committed to the  role and revealed that she did her own  skating for a majority of the movie  she even went as far as to train four  hours a day five days a week over the  course of five months so she could  perfect harding's skating style  she goes out and gives a beautiful skate  this disney plus drama is based off the  true story of teenager zak  zobiak who wrote and performed a  chart-topping song while battling an  aggressive form of cancer  sobiak's family and friends were excited  about a film that celebrated his legacy  and contributed heavily to the film and  even were on set for most of the filming  the soviet family had even donated  zack's real clothes for star fin  argus to wear throughout filming hello  stillwater  the first season of netflix dramedy  received some criticism for its lack of  actors on the spectrum for a  show that's themed around autism  showrunner rabia rashid tried to make up  for this in the second season of the  show  and casted actors who were actually  atypical for the scenes where sam  attends a support group  for people with autism it was because of  this choice that the second season was  much more well received and received  praise for its representation  no chicken fingers that sounds awful you  shouldn't go  elf has become a holiday staple for many  thanks to will ferrell's energetic  performance as buddy the elf  it may come as a surprise to fans that  the scenes of buddy interacting with  everyday new yorkers was entirely  unscripted and many of the people he  interacts with were not actors  what may be the craziest of all is that  farrell really did eat gum  off the city sidewalks in one of the  film's most infamous gags  the guy in the red jogging suit santa  sit  that guy was just there just like elf  home alone is a holiday classic that is  beloved by many  in the scene towards the end of the film  where harry threatens to bite off  kevin's fingers  you may be shocked to learn that joe  pesci really did bite macaulay culkin's  finger  albeit by accident kolkan even claims  that he still has a scar from where  pesci bit him  he had broke the skin and everything i'm  a little nine-year-old boy and he's  going around biting him  out of all the actors who perform their  own stunts tom cruise may just be the  most well known  as he loves to please his fans with some  spectacular stunt work  in this high octane sequence from the  sixth entry in the mission impossible  franchise  cruz performed his most impressive stunt  to date  by actually performing a halo jump and  was skydiving at 200 miles per hour  without a harness  this scene ended up being one 